+# Task: Start-up twins: config defaults and shipped-skill front matter (w50 slice f, RM25) Phase: follow-ups Owner: wave-50 builder f
+
+## Status
+
+Done (2026-10-23), not committed (builder slice; the integrator lands it). Both twins built, read
+at start-up with a digest fallback, checked by their generators' `--check` and the
+`generated_twins` guard. Budgets unchanged. Results and measurements at the end.
+
+Read (reference @ `ab3fe9dffb0a89d534cb795e2a2940e5f6542056`): none — our own start-up path (RM25); the
+pattern is ours from wave 48 (`docs/notes/P25/perf-python.md`, builders e and g; D-16.1084,
+D-16.1090, D-16.1091, D-16.1099).
+Evidence: none.
+
+What it does (own words): two more generated JSON twins on the one-shot start-up path, built the
+way the wave-48 pricing and field-doc twins are (the source stays the source; the twin carries a
+digest; a missing or stale twin costs time, never a wrong answer; a generator with `--check`; the
+`generated_twins` guard runs every `--check`).
+
+1. **Config defaults.** `foundation.config.schema` builds `DEFAULTS` from `ConfigModel()` at
+   import, which forces pydantic to build every config section's validator (~200 ms of import
+   here), and `loader.load` then validates the whole merged tree with `ConfigModel`. Now the
+   section models are deferred (`defer_build=True`, built on first use), `DEFAULTS` is read from
+   `foundation/config/defaults.json` while its sha256 of `schema.py` + `versions.py` matches (else
+   `_build_defaults()` as before), and `validate()` checks only the top-level settings whose value
+   is not exactly (type and value) the default; the defaults are valid by construction (pinned by a
+   test), and anything unusual (a key spelled by field name where an alias exists) takes the old
+   whole-model path. Warnings are the same text in the same order as the whole-model check.
+2. **Shipped-skill front matter.** Every run parses the front matter of the 15 shipped skills (the
+   copies seeded into `<home>/skills`) with the pure-Python YAML loader, ~20 ms. Now
+   `learning/skills/shipped_frontmatter.json` maps the sha256 of each shipped `SKILL.md` front-matter
+   block to its parsed mapping; `split_frontmatter` looks the block's digest up first and parses
+   YAML only on a miss. Keyed by content, so an edited copy, a user skill or a changed shipped
+   skill simply misses; a stale twin can never hand back another text's values.
+
+Inputs → outputs: `uv run python -m indus.foundation.config.defaults_twin [--check]`,
+`uv run python -m indus.learning.skills.frontmatter_twin [--check]` → the two JSON files (exit 1
+with "is stale" on `--check`). Runtime: same `DEFAULTS`, same `validate()` warnings, same
+`ParsedSkill` values, less time.
+
+Files: `src/indus/foundation/config/schema.py`, `.../config/defaults_twin.py`,
+`.../config/defaults.json`; `src/indus/learning/skills/format.py`,
+`.../skills/frontmatter_twin.py`, `.../skills/shipped_frontmatter.json`;
+`tooling/checks/generated_twins.py` + its tests; `biome.json` (skip the two generated JSON
+files like the others); tests under `tests/unit/foundation/config/` and
+`tests/unit/learning/skills/`; `tests/unit/cli/test_oneshot_startup.py`.
+
+Edge cases / failure modes:
+- twin missing, unreadable, not JSON, wrong shape, digest mismatch → slow path (logged at debug);
+- CRLF checkout: sources read as text (universal newlines), so the digest matches either way;
+- a default that JSON cannot carry exactly (tuple, set, date): the generator refuses, so a twin
+  never changes a type; front matter that JSON cannot carry exactly (a YAML date) is left out
+  of the skills twin and parsed as before;
+- `1 == 1.0 == True` in Python: "unchanged from the default" compares type and value, so `0`
+  for a bool setting is still validated;
+- a caller mutating `ParsedSkill.raw`: each hit hands out a fresh copy.
+
+Our design differences / decisions:
+- `W50-f-1` config defaults twin + deferred section models + validate only changed settings.
+- `W50-f-2` shipped-skill front-matter twin keyed by the block's digest (not by path).
+- `W50-f-3` both twins in the `generated_twins` guard; the guard's test fixture also copies
+  `skills/` (the skills generator reads the shipped tree).
+
+Tests we will write:
+- config twin fresh (`--check` 0), equals `_build_defaults()` exactly (types too); import reads the
+  twin and builds no config validator; stale / missing / broken twin → same `DEFAULTS` built from
+  the models; `validate(DEFAULTS) == []`; `validate()` equals the whole-model check on a table of
+  valid, invalid, unknown-key, union and alias inputs.
+- skills twin fresh; covers every shipped skill; a shipped skill's front matter comes from the
+  twin without a YAML parse (counted) and equals the parsed one; an edited block is parsed;
+  hits are independent copies; broken twin → parsed.
+- guard: both new twins checked; a stale one of each fails.
+- one-shot probe: importing the one-shot modules builds no config section validator.
+
+## Decisions for the lead
+- **W50-f-1** config defaults twin. `_Section` and `ConfigModel` set `defer_build=True`;
+  `DEFAULTS` comes from `foundation/config/defaults.json` while its `source_sha256` (sha256 over
+  the names and texts of `schema.py` and `versions.py`, read as text) matches, else from
+  `build_defaults()` (was `_build_defaults`, now public for the generator). `validate()` skips
+  every top-level setting that is absent or `same_value` as its default and validates each other
+  one with a per-setting `TypeAdapter` (the field's annotation plus its constraint metadata, built
+  on first use and kept); `_validate_whole()` is the old whole-model check, kept for a key spelled
+  by field name where an alias exists (`config_version`) and as the oracle the tests compare
+  against. Any edit to `schema.py` (comments too) makes the twin stale: regenerate with
+  `uv run python -m indus.foundation.config.defaults_twin` (the guard says so).
+- **W50-f-2** shipped-skill front-matter twin keyed by the sha256 of the front-matter block (not by
+  path): `format.split_frontmatter` → `frontmatter_block` (the fence split, factored out so the
+  generator splits the same way) → twin lookup → YAML only on a miss; hits are deep copies. The
+  generator reads `bundled_source({})` (never `INDUS_BUNDLED_SKILLS`) and exits 2 when there is
+  no shipped tree; front matter JSON cannot carry exactly goes to `skipped` (none today).
+- **W50-f-3** both generators in `tooling/checks/generated_twins.py` (now four twins); the guard
+  test fixture copies `skills/` beside `src/` because the skills generator reads it; `biome.json`
+  skips the two new generated JSON files like the existing twins (D-16.1102).
+- Budgets unchanged (`tooling/perf/budgets.toml` untouched).
+
+Compare checklist (no reference file; compared against the pre-change behaviour instead):
+- [x] `DEFAULTS` value-, type- and order-identical to the models
+  (`test_defaults_twin.py::test_the_twin_and_defaults_equal_the_models_type_for_type`)
+- [x] stale / missing / broken twin → defaults built from the models
+  (`::test_a_missing_broken_or_stale_twin_builds_the_defaults_from_the_models`,
+  `::test_a_twin_for_other_sources_or_of_the_wrong_shape_is_not_used`)
+- [x] `validate()` warnings identical to the whole-model check, raw and merged with the defaults,
+  over 25 inputs: clean, unknown keys, union `model`, constraint and type errors, bool/int/float
+  look-alikes, the alias and its field name (`::test_validate_matches_the_whole_model_check`);
+  the existing 194 config tests pass unchanged
+- [x] importing the schema / the one-shot modules builds no config model; validating the defaults
+  builds nothing; one changed setting builds one adapter
+  (`::test_importing_the_schema_builds_no_config_validator`,
+  `tests/unit/cli/test_oneshot_startup.py::test_the_one_shot_imports_build_no_config_section_validator`;
+  both fail on main)
+- [x] every shipped skill's raw front matter identical with the twin and with YAML, no YAML call
+  (`test_frontmatter_twin.py::test_shipped_skills_parse_from_the_twin_without_yaml`); an edited
+  block is parsed; hits are independent copies; an unusable twin parses everything; a YAML date
+  is skipped
+- [x] guard: fresh repo has four fresh twins; a stale defaults twin and a stale skills twin each
+  fail (`tooling/checks/tests/test_generated_twins.py`)
+- Deliberate differences: none user-visible.
+- Not taken: `httpx._main` (third party); the remaining ~110 ms of `schema` import is class
+  creation of ~70 section models (fields collected even when deferred).
+
+## Results
+
+Checks (ENV RULE; own `.venv` via `uv sync --locked --offline`; pytest `--basetemp=/tmp/w50f`):
+ruff check / format clean on the touched files; pyright 0 errors on them; lint-imports 1 kept;
+`defaults_twin --check`, `frontmatter_twin --check`, `pricing_twin --check`, `field_docs --check`,
+`indus.protocol.codegen --check` 0; `gen_reference.py --check` fresh; biome check clean (the twins
+skipped); `tooling.checks --require-ref` ok (16 checks, `generated_twins` now four twins; warns
+only: pins placeholder digest, pypdf RS37). pytest `-m "not perf"`: foundation + learning + cli +
+contract + `tooling/checks/tests` 5299 passed, 58 skipped, 1 failed
+(`tests/unit/cli/repl/test_keys.py::test_feed_items_reach_the_screen_through_the_pump`, a 50-try
+settle loop at load ~13; the file passes 37/37 three times alone; it touches neither config
+validation nor skills); web + gateway + service + tools + core + backends + safety + cron +
+providers + protocol 10027 passed, 15 skipped.
+
+Measurements (this 4-core box, shared with other builders; `git archive` of main `7eee12d` vs this
+tree, same venv, alternating, median of 5, the perf test's own workload `fake_runner -z "say
+hello"` to the first stdout byte; load average noted):
+
+| | main | this tree |
+|---|---|---|
+| `import indus.foundation.config.schema`, pydantic preloaded | 199 ms | 131 ms |
+| same, fresh interpreter (pydantic import included), two rounds | 259 / 260 ms | 192 / 182 ms |
+| `validate(DEFAULTS)` after import | 0.6 ms (built at import) | 0.6 ms (builds nothing) |
+| `parse_skill` of the 15 shipped skills | 20.0 / 20.9 ms | 1.0 / 1.1 ms |
+| one-shot first byte, round 1 (load 1.7) | 1365 ms | 1256 ms |
+| one-shot first byte, round 2 (load 1.8) | 1458 ms | 1458 ms |
+| one-shot child CPU, rounds 1 / 2 | 1305 / 1219 ms | 1168 / 1240 ms |
+
+Earlier rounds at load 5–10 were noise-bound (1643 → 1780, 1935 → 1920, 2033 → 2008 ms). The
+pieces are measurable (~70 ms of import, ~20 ms of skill parsing, nothing built by the loader's
+validation); the whole-process number moves inside this box's noise, so judge
+`oneshot_first_token` on a quiet runner (RM25). A one-shot run with the probe in
+`$S/tools/probe_run.py` built no config model and no per-setting adapter, and read the skills
+twin.
+
+Follow-ups: `httpx._main` (third party, ~75 ms); the rest of `schema`'s import is class creation;
+judge RM25 on a clean runner; a contributor editing `schema.py` or a shipped skill must
+regenerate the twin (the guard and the unit tests say which command).
